From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lethalbas <lethalbas@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 19:53:38 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] build(win): emit precompiled-header include from flex %top
 block

The legacy skeletons (Flex.skl, smcFlex.skl) emitted
'#include "StdH.h"' / '#include <Engine/StdH.h>' as the first line of
the generated scanners. With flex's built-in skeleton this is lost and
MSVC fails with C1010 (unexpected end of file while looking for
precompiled header). Restore the include through a %top{} block,
which flex 2.6 places before all generated code.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 Sources/Engine/Base/Scanner.l | 4 ++++
 Sources/Engine/Ska/smcScan.l  | 4 ++++
 2 files changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Sources/Engine/Base/Scanner.l b/Sources/Engine/Base/Scanner.l
index fe991d3e036060b4bb5f267572b9a12229af4de2..fd51475b4398bb610bc1355bd5c410bf11a382d2 100644
--- a/Sources/Engine/Base/Scanner.l
+++ b/Sources/Engine/Base/Scanner.l
@@ -1,3 +1,7 @@
+%top{
+/* SSTRE: flex >= 2.6 built-in skeleton; replaces the precompiled-header include formerly emitted by the legacy skeleton */
+#include "StdH.h"
+}
 %{
 #include "ParsingSymbols.h"
 #include "Parser.h"
diff --git a/Sources/Engine/Ska/smcScan.l b/Sources/Engine/Ska/smcScan.l
index 759907c54f3722d867c91b34b4247add20c1a384..b178610fdbe3c67279b22d9c0c14df499f243f9c 100644
--- a/Sources/Engine/Ska/smcScan.l
+++ b/Sources/Engine/Ska/smcScan.l
@@ -1,3 +1,7 @@
+%top{
+/* SSTRE: flex >= 2.6 built-in skeleton; replaces the precompiled-header include formerly emitted by the legacy skeleton */
+#include <Engine/StdH.h>
+}
 %option prefix="syy"
 %{
 #include "ParsingSmbs.h"
